.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Data files are never committed — parquet, not git, is the right place for
# them, and adjusted-price data is restated over time regardless (spec §4.1).
# The snapshot's MANIFEST.json (hashes, ticker list, row counts, pip freeze)
# IS committed: it is the audit trail that lets anyone verify a copy of the
# actual data they obtain out-of-band, even though re-running the download
# script will NOT reproduce it byte-for-byte (that restatement is exactly
# what "write-once" guards against — a later run is a new snapshot, not a
# reproduction of this one). See DECISIONS.md D-013.
#
# A plain `data/raw/` here would also silently defeat the exception below:
# once git treats a directory itself as ignored it never descends into it to
# apply a nested negation, so `!data/**/MANIFEST.json` alone did nothing.
# `data/raw/*` ignores raw/'s children; re-admitting directories lets git
# look inside them.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/*/
data/raw/*/*
!data/raw/*/MANIFEST.json
data/interim/

# The processed feature/posterior parquet is derived, reproducible data, same
# category as the raw snapshot — not committed (and, unlike the raw snapshot,
# these ARE exactly reproducible: every fitting stage derives its seeds from
# the committed master seed, so re-running a script against the same frozen
# snapshot reproduces them bit-for-bit). `*_schema.json` and `*_summary.json`
# are small, human-readable provenance/results records (schema hash and
# column list; K-selection and evaluation headline numbers) in the same
# spirit as MANIFEST.json, and ARE committed.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/*_schema.json
!data/processed/*_summary.json
data/holdout/

# Generated outputs. reports/figures and reports/logs are regenerated freely
# and not committed — logs in particular would accumulate one file per run.
# reports/tables IS committed for the markdown deliverables that are a named
# review artifact for a build step (the §4.3 QA report, the §5.5 pruning
# report): because the raw snapshot itself cannot be byte-reproduced later
# (D-013), these are the only lasting record of what THIS snapshot produced.
reports/figures/*
reports/logs/*
logs/
!reports/**/.gitkeep

# Model artefacts
*.pt
*.pkl
*.joblib
.Rhistory
